<description>
Move each mirrored bottom source pixel to the far end of its trail and redraw the top half as its reflection.

Input structure
- A solid non-background row separates equal-height top and bottom halves.
- The top half has one marker color on the background.
- In the bottom half, exactly one color has positions that mirror the top markers across the separator, and the other color forms trails touching those source pixels.

Rule
- Identify the bottom source color by reflecting each bottom color into the top half and matching the top marker set.
- For every bottom source pixel, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint.
- Clear the old top markers, bottom sources, and trails; place the source color at each endpoint and place the top marker color at the reflected endpoint.

Key insight
- The top half is only a mirror display of the bottom moving sources; the actual motion is encoded by the trail attached to each bottom source pixel.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "bottom-half source pixels s, identified as the color whose positions reflect to the top marker mask across the separator row",
  "path": "from each s, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint",
  "trajectory": "move s to that endpoint; clear the old source pixel and all trail pixels",
  "transform": "redraw the top marker color at the reflection of each moved source endpoint; keep the separator and background unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: NxN square, N odd, range 7-11 (observed N in {7,9,11})
  layout: top half (rows 0..sep-1) | separator row (sep=(N-1)/2) | bottom half (rows sep+1..N-1)
  colors: 5 distinct -- bg (most frequent), sep_color (fills separator row), top_marker, source, trail; top_marker not in {source, trail}; colors={7,9,5,2,6} [observed]
  separator: solid row of sep_color spanning full width at row sep
  top_half:
    content: K pixels of top_marker color on bg; these mirror the source positions across separator
  bottom_half:
    sources: K pixels of source_color; their reflection (2*sep - r, c) equals the top marker set
    trails: straight 4-connected paths of trail_color, one per source; each trail is adjacent to its source and extends in one cardinal direction (no turns)
    trail_length: 1-4 pixels per trail [observed]
    constraints: trails do not touch each other; endpoints are all distinct; all trail pixels are accounted for by exactly one source
  num_sources: 2-5
  transformation: each source moves to its trail endpoint; trails are erased; top markers updated to reflect new positions

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first (build settled state, then derive input)
  steps:
    1. Choose N from {7, 9, 11} (odd square grid); sep = (N-1)//2
    2. Choose K sources (2-5) and place their endpoint positions in the bottom half (unique cells, on bg)
    3. For each endpoint, pick a cardinal direction and trail length L (1-4); extend L cells in that direction to find the source position (source = trail_end + L steps opposite to trail direction); verify source is in-bounds, on bg, and not colliding with other sources/trails/endpoints
    4. Mark trail cells between source and endpoint (exclusive of both); verify no trail cell collides with another trail or source
    5. Mirror each source position across separator to get top marker positions
    6. Fill grid: bg everywhere, separator row with sep_color, source pixels, trail pixels, top markers
    7. Reject if any constraint violated (collisions, out-of-bounds); retry from step 2
```
